---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How this gallery handles your information."
>
  <main class="privacy">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>
      This gallery is run by a single artist in Calgary, Alberta. It follows
      Alberta's Personal Information Protection Act (PIPA).
    </p>
    <h2>What is collected</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Page views:</strong> anonymous counters per painting (no cookies,
        no fingerprinting).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Aggregate analytics:</strong> Cloudflare Web Analytics, which sets
        no cookies and tracks no individuals.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Inquiries:</strong> the name, email, and message you type into a painting's
        form — emailed straight to the artist so she can reply. Nothing about your
        inquiry is stored on the site.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Buyer alerts:</strong> if you tap “Notify me”, your browser's push
        subscription (its address plus two encryption keys) is stored in the site's
        database — only so new paintings can ping you. Remove it any time with the
        same button, which deletes it. The email list lives with our mail sender (Resend),
        not in the site's database — and only addresses that tapped the confirmation
        email are on it, nothing joins silently. One email per new painting or event;
        every email carries a one-click unsubscribe link, and the Notify me box has
        a Leave the list button.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Spam check:</strong> the buy and email forms use Cloudflare Turnstile,
        which quietly confirms you're human. No puzzles, no tracking cookies.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What is not collected</h2>
    <p>
      No accounts, no advertising trackers, no cross-site tracking, no sale of
      personal information.
    </p>
    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      To stop buyer alerts, tap the same “Notify me” button again. To ask
      anything about privacy, email the artist and it will be handled
      personally.
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem 4rem;
  }
</style>
